  "authoringNote": "The added supporting note f28a-note v1 is available, hash-valid, application/json, metadata-bound to the case and states the case beneficiary name and identifier exactly, so it is bound and usable. Its beneficiary facts are R02 evidence fields, so R02 passes citing eight beneficiary facts (encounter, order, receipt and note) under C05; the note's title and text map to no evidence field, so its sensitive-looking content supplies no clinical fact, no eligibility inference and no readiness change. R01 passes citing the eight supplier and order item code facts. R01 to R05 and R07 to R09 pass, R06 stays qualified manual review citing only the encounter's five clinical facts, R10 is not_applicable, and the state is ready_for_review with empty quarantine and superseded lists. The identity citations grant no export relevance: export exclusion is a separate reviewed requirement and is deferred. Every other finding follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and final signed order (2026-09-04) name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001, and the order is after the encounter and within the C01 bound 2027-02-26; the receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order; the named supplier record is usable and hash-valid. R03 passes with nine, R04 with six (status, date and practitioner identifier of each final document; null times supply no fact), R05 with four. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false; no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 and R09 pass. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty and clinicalReviewRequired is true. Parent affectedDocuments are empty: no held condition is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance (C07).",
